<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annapolis, Maryland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Annapolis is the capital of the US state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>, on the Severn River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chesapeake-bay">Chesapeake Bay</a>. Settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> as Providence in 1649, it became the colonial capital in 1694 and was renamed after Princess Anne. The Congress of the Confederation met there in 1783–1784, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> resigned his command, and it has been home to the US Naval Academy since 1845.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/annapolis-maryland.jpg" alt="Annapolis, Maryland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flickr user: high limitzz https://www.flickr.com/people/highlimitstudio/ · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Some_Annapolis_commercial_strip.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
